Ingress Resource: A YAML declaration defining HTTP rules (e.g., api.example.com goes to api-service, /store goes to shop-service).

Ingress Controller: The actual running daemon (usually an Nginx, Traefik, or Envoy reverse proxy) that watches the API server for Ingress rules and routes network packets.

Internet Traffic (HTTP: 80 / HTTPS: 443)
                          |
                          v
        +-----------------------------------+
        |      Ingress Controller Pod       | (e.g., ingress-nginx)
        +-----------------+-----------------+
                          |
             Path-based Routing Evaluation
             +------------+------------+
             |                         |
       Path: /apple              Path: /banana
             |                         |
             v                         v
   +-------------------+     +-------------------+
   |  apple-service    |     |  banana-service   | (ClusterIP: Port 80)
   +---------+---------+     +---------+---------+
             |                         |
             v                         v
     [ apple pods ]            [ banana pods ]

     